>Boring Gehennon isn't about the distance, it's about the variety.

And in this patch I would submit there is variety -- there are only a
certain number of levels and there is an encounter with a major demon
or some other feature (entrance to branch, tower) on almost every
single level.

The reason *I* find Gehennom boring is because I spend forever walking
around empty, featureless corridors looking for the one or two really
important items I need for my ascension kit.

This patch cuts out both of those difficulties with one stroke -- it
cuts radically down on the otherwise-empty maze levels. And since a
problem with cutting down the maze levels is that it gives you less
chance of finding an important object, I added the additional change as
described.  That way,  you still get the Ascension items you would
otherwise be cheated out of by losing 10 or more levels, but you don't
get weighed down with tons of scrolls of create monster, daggers,
chunks of worthless glass, etc.

I would say that 90% of the loot on a level is utterly worthless, but I
still have to sift through it to get my ascension items. This cuts down
on the sifting time and eliminates much of the time spent in
featureless corridors with generic monsters while increasing the time
you'll be facing off with major enemies.

That's also why I didn't increase the number of shops in Orcus town --
because most likely you would just get a bunch of additional mimics and
crud like throwing spears rather than the important things you
absolutely need.

*Shrug* we'll see if it works.  If it doesn't, I can always re-write
it. 

